                    },
                    "authorAssociation": "MEMBER",
                    "body": "> Would be a lot simpler than copy pasting an internal function + adding an autocmd.\r\n\r\nNo internal function is needed for `go_in_plus` action (and for most other built-in actions, for that matter). [`MiniFiles.go_in()`](https://nvim-mini.org/mini.nvim/doc/mini-files.html#minifiles.go_in) supports `close_on_file` option which can be set to `true` to have `go_in_plus` behavior.\r\n\r\nThe autocommand approach is already present and a lot more flexible than making configuration code more complex. So although the \"multiple people suggested\" is a valid reasoning (if not taking prior searching of issues into account), I don't think I like the idea of allowing multiple keys per action in the `MiniFiles.config` itself.",
                    "bodyHTML": "<blockquote>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Would be a lot simpler than copy pasting an internal function + adding an autocmd.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p dir=\"auto\">No internal function is needed for <code class=\"notranslate\">go_in_plus</code> action (and for most other built-in actions, for that matter). <a href=\"https://nvim-mini.org/mini.nvim/doc/mini-files.html#minifiles.go_in\" rel=\"nofollow\"><code class=\"notranslate\">MiniFiles.go_in()</code></a> supports <code class=\"notranslate\">close_on_file</code> option which can be set to <code class=\"notranslate\">true</code> to have <code class=\"notranslate\">go_in_plus</code> behavior.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">The autocommand approach is already present and a lot more flexible than making configuration code more complex. So although the \"multiple people suggested\" is a valid reasoning (if not taking prior searching of issues into account), I don't think I like the idea of allowing multiple keys per action in the <code class=\"notranslate\">MiniFiles.config</code> itself.</p>",
                    "bodyText": "Would be a lot simpler than copy pasting an internal function + adding an autocmd.\n\nNo internal function is needed for go_in_plus action (and for most other built-in actions, for that matter). MiniFiles.go_in() supports close_on_file option which can be set to true to have go_in_plus behavior.\nThe autocommand approach is already present and a lot more flexible than making configuration code more complex. So although the \"multiple people suggested\" is a valid reasoning (if not taking prior searching of issues into account), I don't think I like the idea of allowing multiple keys per action in the MiniFiles.config itself.",
